/** \defgroup ASSEMBLY Assembly
 *  \ingroup PYTHONWORKBENCHES
 *  \brief Tools to build assemblies
 *
 *  Assembly links can be expanded in three load modes:
 *  - Normal: fully load the linked assembly and solve all internal joints.
 *  - Auto: switch to lightweight behavior once the linked assembly reaches the
 *    user-configured large assembly threshold.
 *  - Lightweight: keep the linked document partially loaded and suppress
 *    internal joint expansion for faster navigation in large projects.
 *
 *  The large assembly threshold is configured in the Assembly preferences.
 *  Setting the threshold to 0 disables the automatic switch used by Auto mode.
 *
 *  When an `AssemblyLink` comes from a lightweight STEP workspace, double-click
 *  now reloads the cached shard document automatically when needed. The same
 *  links expose context-menu actions to load or unload the shard explicitly,
 *  can open a live metrics dock for the workspace, and unloaded shards keep a
 *  lightweight bounding-box proxy in the master assembly for navigation and
 *  selection context. With a shard budget of 0, the master workspace starts
 *  with every shard unloaded and only reloads geometry on demand. With spare
 *  shard budget, loading one workspace link can also prefetch spatially
 *  nearby shard links automatically to reduce follow-up load latency while
 *  browsing large assemblies. The view-aware optimizer waits for a short idle
 *  window after camera motion before rebalancing shard loads so viewport
 *  navigation does not stutter because of synchronous shard open/close work.
 *  It also culls far lightweight proxy placeholders continuously from the
 *  active view while navigating, retains shards based on current frustum
 *  intersection and focus
 *  distance, applies a short hysteresis window before trimming edge-of-view
 *  shards, and can warm-prefetch one extra nearby shard once the camera stays
 *  stable long enough. The same idle loop also restores the deferred initial
 *  shard budget for user-saved lightweight `.FCStd` workspaces near the
 *  current camera focus, avoiding a synchronous shard reopen burst during
 *  document restore.
 *  Import runtime status can be used to inspect how many links are
 *  still proxies and which shard loads were manual, prefetched, or trimmed
 *  during the current session, and the metrics dock surfaces the same counters
 *  live in the GUI while also allowing direct load, unload, explicit nearby
 *  prefetch, live budget tuning, and trim actions on workspace shards.
 *  Individual shards can also be pinned for the current workspace and the
 *  pinning state is persisted in the lightweight cache so automatic trim
 *  passes keep key sub-assemblies loaded across reopen. Reopen and live budget
 *  changes still honor the configured shard budget, automatically restoring
 *  pinned shards when possible and prioritizing the most recent pinned shards
 *  first when the budget cannot accommodate them all.
 *
 *  For tuning and regression checks on large synthetic models, use
 *  `AssemblyTests/LargeAssemblyBenchmark.py`. It can be run with FreeCADCmd to
 *  compare recompute cost and lightweight behavior across different component
 *  counts, thresholds, and load modes.
 *
 *  For manual GUI review, `AssemblyTests/PrepareLargeAssemblyReview.py`
 *  creates below-threshold and above-threshold `AssemblyLink` scenarios that
 *  make it easier to inspect `Normal`, `Auto`, and `Lightweight` behavior.
 */
